<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45233" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stagno</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a.
		stagnum = stannum; cf. stagneus, s. v. stanneus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>to overlay</i> or <i>plate with</i> stannum (post-class.),
					<i><span class="en">Plin. Val. 1, 31 <i>med.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 4</span></i>
			<i>med.</i> —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to make fast</i>,
				<i>strengthen</i>, <i>fortify</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">se adversus insidias,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					37, 2, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">potionibus stagnata animalia,</span>”
				<i>strengthened</i>, <i>invigorated</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. 1, 18 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 2, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
